    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d708">

                <pb facs="0703" n="1437" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1437"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mavroyeni Bey.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-12-30"><hi rendition="#italic">December 30,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 62.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 27th instant, in which, in view of an unfavorable report
                    alleged to have been made to this Department by Mr. Chilton on occurrences at
                    Trebizond, you inclose, by way of information merely, the report of the local
                    authorities of Trebizond, making it appear that force of arms had to be resorted
                    to in order to put down rebellion of Armenians.</p>
                <p>Mr. Chilton’s reports of events of which he was an eyewitness during his stay in
                    Trebizond have not been printed, and the statement in <pb facs="0704" n="1438"
                        xml:id="pg1438"/> the press that they were “rather unfavorable to the
                    Turkish authorities” was not authorized. The Department is satisfied of the
                    impartial fidelity of the narratives furnished to it by Mr. Chilton.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
